### URL Feature API Tests
### Base URL: http://localhost:3000/api/url

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/url
@token = your-auth-token-here
@domain = your-domain.com
@alias = your-alias

### 1. Get Short URL Info
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{domain}}/{{alias}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 2. Create Short URL
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "original_url": "https://www.example.com/very-long-url-that-needs-to-be-shortened",
  "domain": "{{domain}}",
  "alias": "{{alias}}",
  "description": "Example URL for testing"
}

###

### 3. Create URL with minimal data (auto-generated alias)
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "original_url": "https://www.minimal-example.com",
  "domain": "{{domain}}"
}

###

### 4. Create URL with empty domain (uses default)
POST {{baseUrl}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "original_url": "https://www.example.com",
  "domain": ""
}

###

### 5. Update Short URL
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/{{domain}}/{{alias}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "original_url": "https://www.example.com/updated-very-long-url-that-needs-to-be-shortened"
}

###

### 6. Delete Short URL
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{domain}}/{{alias}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 7. Test without authorization (should fail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{domain}}/{{alias}}

###

### 8. Test with invalid domain/alias
GET {{baseUrl}}/invalid-domain/invalid-alias
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
